    software like Aldus PageMaker including versions of Lorem Ipsum
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>Notice:</p>
<p>In the example above if you move with i.e: two pointers (fingers) the moved distance will double. If that is a disturbance for you, implement the <code>ev.isPrimary</code> boolean into the <code>move()</code> function's logic.</p>
<p>Additional reading:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Pointer_events" rel="noreferrer">API Pointer_events</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/setPointerCapture" rel="noreferrer">Element setPointerCapture</a></li>
</ul>

Q: Select Query and will appear to comboBox in Netbeans &amp; mysql A: <p>try using an arrayList !! it will give you a push like effect</p>

<p>something like this</p>

<pre><code>    ArrayList&lt;String&gt; categories = new ArrayList&lt;&gt;();
    Connection conn = null;
    Statement stmt = null;
    ResultSet rs = null;
    try {
        System.out.println("\ntrying connection");
        conn = DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:mysql://localhost/products?user=root&amp;password=");
        stmt = conn.createStatement();
        rs = stmt.executeQuery("SELECT DISTINCT categorie FROM product");
        while (rs.next()) {
            categories.add(rs.getString(1));
        }
        for (String item : categories) {
            ComboBoxCategorie.addItem(item);
        }

    } catch (SQLException ex) {
        System.out.println("SQLException: " + ex.getMessage());
        System.out.println("SQLState: " + ex.getSQLState());
        System.out.println("VendorError: " + ex.getErrorCode());
    } finally {
        if (stmt != null) {
            try {
                stmt.close();
            } catch (SQLException sqlEx) {
            } // ignore
            stmt = null;
        }
    }
</code></pre>

<p>you can ignore the catch and finally clause!! just close the stmt</p>

Q: TYPO3 Extbase extension plugins: reveal CE data object in Fluid templates A: <blockquote>
<p>But Extbase Plugins now work like an actual content element
Extbase plugins added to <code>tt_content</code> always have been a content element, unrelated to main-type (ctype) or sub-type ( ctype=liste, list_type).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Usually extbase plugin renders their own things and need to pass down to the view (assign it) what is required or should be needed. TYPO3 does not provide
it and if you need it, add it.</p>
<p>If you want to reuse the <code>FSC</code>(fluid-styled-content`) partials like the header, you also need to create a record representation yourself in the plugin.</p>
<p>Some CONTENT_OBJECTS(TypoScript) add these informations, but not all like extbase plugins or any USER_INT element (extbase is that kind of content element, only that TYPO3 Extbases adds a handler for it doing some magic stuff).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>And I’d like to know how this is best be done.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You already got the answer, Peter Kraume already posted what you need to add to the extbase controller action and assign it to the view (or use the generic initializeAction() method so it's done for all of them - than you can use it.</p>
<p>Not tested, but I think DataProcessers does not have an effect on a extbase plugin which creates the view itself and the rendereing and not the outside content element.</p>
<p>For TYPO3 v14 if you want to have record like things in it you <strong>may</strong> add following to your action(s) or <code>initializeAction()</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>$this-&gt;view-&gt;assignMultiple([
    'data' =&gt; $this-&gt;getCurrentContentObjectRenderer()?-&gt;data,
    'record' =&gt; $this-&gt;getCurrentContentRecord($this-&gt;getCurrentContentObjectRenderer()),
]);
</code></pre>
<p>and add following two methods to your controller (or create a trait to use the trait and avoid duplicated code):</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>protected function getCurrentContentObjectRenderer(): ?ContentObjectRenderer
{
    return $this-&gt;request-&gt;getAttribute('currentContentObject');
}

protected function getCurrentContentRecord(?ContentObjectRenderer $contentObjectRenderer): ?RecordInterface
{
    $row = $contentObjectRenderer?-&gt;data;
    if (!is_array($row) || $row === []) {
        return null;
    }

    return GeneralUtility::makeInstance(RecordFactory::class)
        -&gt;createResolvedRecordFromDatabaseRow('tt_content', $row);
}
</code></pre>
